1. What is Git/ Source Code Management ?

Git means Global Information Tool. It is free and open source.
Git is a version control system (VCS) or Source Code Management (SCM).
It is used to track the files.
It is a platform independent tool.
We can maintain multiple versions of same file.
It is written in C programming on 2005 by Linus Torvalds.

-----------------------------

2. Why Git?

Git tracks changes we made, so we have a record of what we done or who and when changes made. 
We can revert to specific versions, it makes collaboration easy, allowing changes by multiple people to all merged into one source.

