6. What are Git stages?

There are 3 stages in Git:
1. Working directory:- Initially you create a files that is present in this working directory. Git is only aware of having files in the project.
It will not track the files. If you want to track a file then we have to use git add.
2. Staging area:- It contains all tracking files. It is like a playground to developers. They can add code or remove code anything they can do. Once modifications are done next we can save the changes then give git commit.
3. Repository:-  It contains our project final code, When we commit the file it will store in repository.
It contains collection of files and history of changes made to those files.

We have two types of repository. 1. Local 2. Remote

-------------------------

7. What is git status?

Git status is used to know the tracking and untracking files in our server.

---------------------------

8. How to track a file in Git?

To track a file in git we use git add filename.
Once we add file moves to staging area and it gets started tracking, so that we know every modifications of the file.

----------------------------------

9. How to commit a file?

To commit a file we use command called git commit -m "message" filename. 
Without commit message we can't commit the file.
Once we commit the file it will not show in git status. After if you have done some modifications then only it will show in status.

------------------------

10. What is git log?

We can see list of all commits. Recent commits will always show on top. It will show author name, date, time and commit message. 
For every commit it will always generate automatic unique id. 

---------------------------------------

11. How to configure in Git?

To change root/author name and change email we have to do configure.
git config user.name "username"
git config user.email "email"

---------------------

12. What is git show?

To see complete information, who made changes, added new lines or deleted code, time and commit message everything we can see.

