13.  What is git amend/ How to change the commit message?

Amend is used to change the commit information(author name Or commit message). 
To change author details git commit --amend --author "username <email>"
To change commit message: git commit --amend -m "commit message"
,commit id will automatically get changed. It will work only for latest commit.
We can also attach all the files which are present in staging area to the previous commit using amend command: git commit --amend --no-edit

------------------------
14. How to send the files from staging area to working directory? (OR) How to untrack the file?

To untrack a file we use command called: git rm --cached filename

-----------------------------------------

15. What is .gitignore?

If you kept a file or folder in .gitignore file it will not track until you removed. If you want to track the files which is present in .gitignore we use command called: git add -f *
Once you kept file in .gitignore, when you give ll command you will see filename, but when you check in git status it will not show until and unless you remove from .gitignore

-----------------------------------

16. What is git reset soft and git reset hard?

Soft command is used to delete only commit. git reset --soft HEAD~1 (top 1 commit will get deleted)

Hard command is used to delete commit and its action.  git reset --hard HEAD~1 (top 1 commit and its action gets deleted)

---------------------------------

17. What is git reflog?

Git reflog is used to see list of all commits as well as deleted commits.

-----------------------------------

18. What is Cherry pick? 

We can use cherry-pick in two ways.
1. By using cherry-pick we can get back deleted commits. After restoring deleted commit, commit id will automatically change.
  git cherry-pick commit_id (If you forgot to note commit id by git reflog you will get all commits including deleted commits, based on commit message you can select the commit id)

2. If we want to take only few commits to another branch we will give specific commit ids. git cherry-pick commit_id1 commit_id2 ......

